INSTALLING REPYCUDD
-------------------

PyPI has wheels for Linux, macOS and 64-bit Windows, so usually

    python -m pip install repycudd

is all you need. The rest of this file is about building from source.

repycudd builds with pip on Linux, macOS and 64-bit Windows (CI covers all
three). CUDD 3.0.0 is vendored in cudd-3.0.0/ and linked statically into the
extension, so there is nothing else to install.

Requirements:
  - Python 3.9 or later, with pip.
  - A C/C++ compiler: gcc or clang on Linux and macOS, Microsoft Visual C++
    14.0 or later on Windows ("Build Tools for Visual Studio", C++ workload).
  - SWIG >= 4.2. pip fetches it from PyPI automatically.

Install into the current environment:

    python -m pip install .

Or into a plain directory:

    python -m pip install --no-deps --target <dir> .

and then put <dir> on PYTHONPATH.

On CPython (except the free-threaded builds) the extension uses the stable
ABI, so the same build works on every CPython from 3.9 on.

The CUDD sources carry local patches so that pointers are never stored in a
`long`, which is 32 bits on 64-bit Windows.

BREL support (brel.i) is not built.

